--- body ---
## Context

Skills name other skills in Claude Code syntax: `` `/name` `` (145 sites in
`skills/*/SKILL.md` on 2026-10-26, against 21 "the X skill") and the tool call
`Skill(skill: "x", args: …)` (one file left, `skills/gaze/references/battery.md`,
after hunt and raid were rewritten on branch edit-skills-1979616). Codex and Pi
load the same skill bodies but do not slash-invoke them; `rules/authoring-skills.md`
asks to name capabilities, not the tool. A Codex model most likely reads
`/verify-adherence` as a name, so the cost today is ambiguity, not breakage.

## What to do

Rewrite skill references in `skills/` and `rules/` as plain names ("run the
verify-adherence skill", "load the hunt skill with `<id> inline`"). Keep `/name`
where the text addresses the author typing a command. Then add a
`check-agnostic.sh` skill pattern for `Skill(skill` so the tool syntax does not
come back.

## Relevant files

- `skills/*/SKILL.md`, `skills/*/references/*.md`, `rules/*.md`
- `scripts/check-agnostic.sh`
- `skills/harness-doctor/references/authoring-skills.md` (state the convention in one line; `rules/authoring-skills.md` is now its edit-time stub)

## Test

`check-agnostic.sh` fails on a fixture skill containing `Skill(skill:` and passes
on the rewritten tree.

## Exit criteria

- No `Skill(skill` in `skills/` or `rules/`; `check-agnostic.sh` flags it.
- Model-facing skill references use plain names; any `/name` left addresses the author.
- `skills/harness-doctor/references/authoring-skills.md` states the convention.
